## Where it fits in the sequence

**During.** A single rescue boat has a fixed passenger capacity. Towing cabins behind it is proposed as a way to move more people in each cycle, with the crew still in control of the boat.

**After.** Traditional evacuations end at dry land, where families wait for shelter to arrive. The proposal is that the cabin that carried a family becomes its first protection on land: one deployment, continuous protection.

## Status

AeroCabin™ is presented on this site as a proposed capability. Demonstrations with response teams, and any deployment carried out by the Foundation, will be recorded under [Our Actions](/our-actions) with dates, participants and photographs. Images on this page are concept renders and are labeled as such.

## How a community campaign works

A community, a fire company or a group of neighbors can ask CMAX Foundation to open a campaign for a specific department. The Foundation confirms the recipient institution before the campaign uses its name, keeps the campaign page updated, and coordinates the formal delivery once the goal is met.
